{"id":"civicplus-42-11132024-191","platform":"civicplus","body":"Priority Setting Ad Hoc Committee","name":"Priority Setting Ad Hoc Committee Liaison Meeting Agenda","date":"2024-11-13","time":"","canceled":false,"agenda_url":"https://www.beverlyhills.org/AgendaCenter/ViewFile/Agenda/_11132024-191","minutes_url":"https://www.beverlyhills.org/AgendaCenter/ViewFile/Minutes/_11132024-191","packet_url":"","category_id":42,"agenda_text":"Beverly Hills City Council Liaison I Priority Setting Ad Hoc Committee\n  will conduct a Special Meeting, at the following time and place, and will address the\n  agenda listed below:\n\n  CITY OF BEVERLY HILLS\n  455 N. Rexford Drive\n  Room 280A\n  Beverly Hills, CA 90210\n\n  IN-PERSON I TELEPHONIC I VIDEO CONFERENCE MEETING\n\n  Beverly Hills Liaison Committee Meeting\n  https :llbeverlyhills-orq .zoom uslmylcommittee\n  .\n\n  Meeting ID: 516 191 2424\n  Passcode: 90210\n\n  You can also dial in by phone:\n  +1 669 900 9128 US\n  +1 833 548 0282 (Toll-Free)\n\n  One tap mobile:\n  +1 66990091 28,,51 61 912424# us\n  +1 8335480282,,51 6191 2424# US (Toll-Free)\n\n  Wednesday, November 13, 2024\n  2:00 PM\n\nPlease be advised that pre-entry metal detector screening requirements are now in place\nin City HalL Members of the public are requested to plan visits accordingly.\n\nIn the interest of maintaining appropriate social distancing, members of the public can view this\nmeeting through live webcast at www.beverlyhills.org/live and on BH Channel 10 or Channel 35\non Spectrum Cable, and can participate in the teleconference/video conference by using the link\nabove. Written comments may be emailed to mayorandcitycouncil(beverlyhiIls.org and will also\nbe taken during the meeting when the topic is being reviewed by the Beverly Hills City Council\nLiaison / Priority Setting Ad Hoc Committee. Beverly Hills Liaison meetings will be in-person at\nCity Hall.\n\n  AGENDA\n\n  1) Public Comment\n  a. Members of the public will be given the opportunity to directly address the\n  Committee on any item listed on the agenda.\n\n  2) Review draft priorities for Fiscal Year 2025 2026\n  -\n\f  3) Adjournment\n\nHuma Ahmed\nCity Clerk\n\nPosted: November 8, 2024\n\nPursuant to the Americans with Disabilities Act, the City of Beverly Hills will make reasonable\nefforts to accommodate persons with disabilities. If you require special assistance, please call\n(310) 285-1014 (voice) or (310) 285-6881 (TTY). Providing at least twenty-four (24) hours\nadvance notice will help to ensure availability of services. City Hall, Room 280A is wheelchair\naccessible.\n\n  2\n\f  CITY OF BEVERLY HILLS\n\n  POLICY AND MANAGEMENT\n\n  MEMORANDUM\n\n TO:  Priority Setting Ad Hoc (Vice Mayor Nazarian and Councilmember Corman)\n\n FROM:  Nancy Hunt-Coffey, City Manager\n\n DATE:  November 13, 2024\n\n SUBJECT:  Review draft priorities for fiscal year 2025-26\n\nAs noted previously, the City Council previously authorized the ad hoc to work with staff to develop\na list of proposed strategic priority areas, associated draft goals and work plan items for fiscal\nyear 2025-26, and asked that the final draft priorities return to the City Council in the fall for\nadoption.\n\nToward this end, staff developed the draft priorities, goals and work plan items which are included\nin Attachment 1. For the most part, the priorities were listed if they require substantial investment\nby the City, in terms of capital and/or staff time, and/or they will have a meaningful impact on the\ncommunity. On October 28, 2024 the ad hoc made good progress in reviewing the proposed list.\nThe edits on the items on Attachment 1 represent the comments and edits made at the October\nmeeting. The ad hoc is asked to continue their work reviewing the draft priorities, goals and work\nplan items.\n\nRecommendation\nThe Council ad hoc members are asked to provide feedback on the attached draft priorities,\ngoals, and work plan items for fiscal year 2025-26. Once these items are finalized by the ad\nhoc, they will be brought to the full City Council.\n\f  DRAFT\n  City of Beverly Hills\n  Strategic Priorities, Goals and Work Plans\n\n**Provide a distinction between items that Council has already approved in concept versus items that\nCouncil hasn’t yet reviewed.\n\n  •  SP1: Enhance Community Health Safety and Safety Health\n  o G1.1: Prepare for opening of Metro stations\n  ▪ WP1.1.1: Location Pending Build Beverly Hills Police Department\n  (BHPD) kiosk at La Cienega Metro Station.\n  ▪ WP1.1.2: Implement security model/staffingBHPD sworn staffing model\n  for La Cienega Metro Station.\n  ▪ WP1.1.3: Build out security model for Beverly Metro Station.\n  o G1.2: Ensure safe buildings\n  ▪ WP1.2.1: Complete triennial building code update (to be effective 1/1/26)\n  o G1.3: Increase pedestrian safety\n  ▪ WP1.3.1: Add or reconfigure crosswalks at multiple locations\n  (Wilshire/LeDoux, Olympic between Wetherly and Almont, 6-way\n  intersection, etc.) and right turn slip lanes. ** Clarify if this overlaps with\n  7.1.2 and whether it fits better into SP7.\n  ▪ Investigate putting pedestrian islands on certain streets to prevent tourists\n  taking pictures from being hit by cars.\n  ▪ Investigate putting pedestrian islands on certain streets to prevent tourists\n  taking photographs from being hit by cars.\n  o G1.4: Continue emergency preparations\n  ▪ WP1.4.1: Revise Information Technology business continuity plans to\n  include updating and standardizing critical documentation.\n  o G1.5: Implement new technologies to support public safety **Move this item\n  higher in the list to emphasize its importance.\n  ▪ WP1.5.1: Pending City Council Direction Cloud Migration/upgrade and\n  eRecords Management System (RMS) upgrade for BHPD and Beverly\n  Hills Fire Department (BHFD)\n  ▪ WP1.5.2: Pending City Council Direction Expand drone coverage to 24/7\n  ▪ WP1.5.3 Continue to expand number of closed-circuit television (CCTV)\n  cameras and automated License Plate Readers (ALPRs)\n  ▪ WP1.5.4: Expand and enhance public safety technology to include training\n  and digital forensics software, e.g. Force Metrics Dataminr.\n  ▪ WP1.5.5: Expand automated vehicle location (AVL) system for real time\n  vehicle location for BHPD and BHFA. Allows for dispatch of closest\n  resource.\n  ▪ WP1.5.6: Expand use of artificial intelligence (A/I) based public safety\n  applications particularly related to video searching e.g. Veritone\n\n  1\n\f  ▪WP1.5.7: Expand cyber security posture by expanding National Institute\n  of Standards & Technology (NIST) cyber security standards and plan\n  development, expand information technology inventory management\n  (ITIM), and provide end-user best-practices training\n  ▪ WP1.5.8: Complete upgrade of technology in Emergency Operations\n  Center and examine location of the EOC.\n  ▪ WP1.5.9: Implement AXON My90 software which will allow residents to\n  track the status of their calls for service to BHPD. **Include more dtail\n  about AXON My90 software and what it would do.\n  o G1.6: Adjust staffing needs to respond to community need\n  ▪ WP1.6.1: Pending City Council Direction Study use of nonsworn\n  Community Security Service Officers for Metro and other locations\n\n- SP2: Practice Effective and Transparent Governance\n  o G2.1: Hire and retain talented employees\n  ▪ WP2.1.1: Conduct comprehensive class and compensation study\n  o G2.2: Improve Internal systems\n  ▪ WP2.2.1: Award and implement budget book production software\n  o G2.3: Ensure effective transition of Council responsibilities\n  ▪ WP2.3.1: Install new Mayor/Vice Mayor in April 2026\n  ▪ WP2.3.2: Conduct municipal election in June 2026\n  ▪ Carry out Mayor initiatives—TBD & incorporated into priorities\n  o G2.4: Expand public-facing eGov offerings\n  ▪ WP2.4.1: Automate paper-based counter transactions including fire\n  department-related permits, planning application submissions, special\n  events, and forms automation\n  ▪ WP2.4.2: Upgrade customer relations management (CRM) and call-center\n  software offerings to support AskBH and departments with customer\n  service operations. **Elaborate on what this item entails\n  ▪ WP2.4.3: Expand online permitting capabilities through enhancements to\n  existing systems, e.g. Citysmart\n  ▪ WP2.4.4: Pending City Council Direction Expand A/I-based software\n  offerings, including a customer service chat bot, productivity tools (e.g.\n  CoPilot, staff report automation), and development-records search\n  ▪ WP2.4.5: Upgrade and expand customer-facing applications including\n  library systems, rec and park reservation systema, and utility billing /\n  water management systems, and property information system\n  ▪ WP2.4.6: Upgrade and expand internal efficiency software, including\n  agenda automation, Public Records Act request (PRAR) facilitation,\n  lobbyist registration management, budget development tools, and financial\n  reporting. Ensure that any use of AI would be reviewed by a human before\n  information is made available to the public.\n\n  2\n\f-  SP3: Ensure Financial Stability and Economically Sustainable Growth\n  o G3.1: Ensure responsible fiscal stewardship **Clarify comment regarding the\n  value of the City’s assets/art.\n  ▪ WP3.1.1: Continue developing and implementing cost saving measures\n  and revenue enhancement ideas proposed from the Blue-Ribbon\n  Committee/Audit & Finance Committee based on overall City Council\n  direction\n  ▪ WP3.1.2: Pending City Council directionDirection Initiate comprehensive\n  Citywide Fee Study and fee database development (including feasibility of\n  different fees for affordable housing)\n  ▪ WP3.1.3: Pending City Council directionDirection Consider the\n  development of impact fees\n  ▪ WP3.1.4: Enhance Charitable Foundations’ role to include soliciting\n  donations and developing a sponsorship program for events\n  ▪ WP3.1.5: Conduct off street and on street parking rate study.**Clarify\n  what this would entail.\n  ▪ WP3.1.6: Study the City’s telework program for its effectiveness and as a\n  recruitment tool.\n\n-  SP4: Augment Community Quality of Life\n  o G4.1: Provide programs and services that respond to the needs of the community\n  ▪ WP4.1.1: Restructure Community Assistance Grant Fund Program\n  o G4.2: Provide programs and spaces that benefit the residents of the City\n  ▪ WP4.2.1: Work w/school district to further develop Early Childhood\n  Education Center at Hawthorne School\n  ▪ WP4.2.2: Begin planning for reintroduction of Peters and Salter Theaters\n  at the high school as well as the Konheim building\n  ▪ WP4.2.3: Pending additional funding Arts and Culture Commission\n  workplan item – Festival Beverly Hills\n  ▪ WP4.2.4: Arts and Culture Commission workplan item – Artwalks\n  ▪ WP4.2.5: Develop a plan to expand Library program offerings, TBD.\n  ▪ WP4.2.6: Pending City Council Direction Plan and implement,\n  programming, events, and activities, that bring the community together\n  around the celebration of the Nowruz holiday\n  ▪ WP4.2.7: Pending City Council Direction Plan and implement,\n  programming, events, and activities, that bring the community together\n  around the 4th of July Independence Day\n  ▪ WP4.2.8: Continue to identify cultural and performing arts opportunities\n  for residents and the public to experience the arts in person, at the historic,\n  restored, Greystone Theater\n  ▪ WP4.2.9: Pending City Council Direction Human Relations Commission\n  Workplan – Continue to expand Day of Wellness event at Roxbury Park\n  working with Health and Safety and Recreation and Parks Commissions.\n\n  3\n\f  ▪  WP4.2.10: Prepare for 2028 Olympics related to security, transportation,\n  programming, etc.\n  ▪ WP4.2.11: Pending City Council Direction Human Relations Commission\n  Workplan--Critical Conversations\n  o  G4.3: Improve Public Spaces\n  ▪ WP4.3.1: Pending City Council Direction Complete renovation and\n  replacement of play equipment at La Cienega playground\n  ▪ WP4.3.2: Arts and Culture Commission Workplan--Continue working\n  with the Arts and Culture Commission and the Fine Art Acquisition Work\n  Plan, on the acquisition, installation, and restoration of the City’s fine art\n  collection\n  ▪ WP4.3.3: Pending City Council Direction Renovate public first floor\n  Library restrooms\n  ▪ WP4.3.4: Complete Paley Center for Media archive move in at Beverly\n  Hills Public Library\n\n-  SP5: Maintenance and Develop Infrastructure and Facilities\n  o G5.1: Maintain Public Facilities & Infrastructure\n  ▪ WP5.1.1: Replace Civic Center chilled water line\n  ▪ WP5.1.2: Complete improvements of Library fire alarm upgrade\n  ▪ WP5.1.3: Complete reconstruction of Will Rogers Park restroom and\n  upgrade the water feature.\n  ▪ WP5.1.4: Complete partial roof replacement at 331 Foothill Rd. building\n  ▪ WP5.1.5: Pending City Council Direction Facade and seismic upgrades to\n  parking structures\n  ▪ WP5.1.6: Complete Coldwater Canyon Drive restoration and restriping\n  ▪ WP5.1.7: Complete lower Greystone drainage & access road\n  reconstruction\n  ▪ WP5.1.8: Develop master plan for police station improvements\n  ▪ WP5.1.9: Replace IT data center heating, ventilation and air conditioning\n  (HVAC) and uninterruptible power supply (UPS) Systems\n  ▪ WP5.1.10: Renovate Planning Department and City Clerk’s office\n  ▪ WP5.1.11: Expand Fire station #2 for new bedrooms to include 2 new\n  individual bedrooms to accommodate personnel assigned to the Station.\n  ▪ WP5.1.12: Expand wireless data networks—wifi at the parks & for public\n  events.\n  ▪ WP5.1.13: Street resurfacing associated with Metro projects, including\n  Wilshire Blvd. and residential areas affected by dewatering wells and/or\n  haul route violations\n  o G5.2: Develop New Facilities\n  ▪ WP5.2.1: Install new Automatic Transfer Switch at Main Point of Entry at\n  City Hall bridge for emergency power\n\n  4\n\f  ▪ WP5.2.2: Implement streetscape enhancements per Connect BH on\n  Wilshire and La Cienega Blvds., including new or enhanced crosswalks,\n  transit shelters and bikeway improvements\n  ▪ WP5.2.3: Pending City Council Direction Complete construction of dog\n  park shade structure & resurfacing\n  ▪ WP5.2.4: Pending City Council Direction - Recreation and Parks\n  Commission Workplan Complete selection of dedicated courts to be\n  resurfaced for pickleball. Develop and implement registration system and\n  rules associated with pickleball.\n  ▪ WP5.2.5: Pending City Council Direction Work with community\n  committee and artist to construct October 7th permanent memorial\n  o G5.3: Upgrade key IT infrastructure\n  ▪ WP5.3.1: Upgrade cable television back-end infrastructure by\n  streamlining and centralizing audio, video, and control systems in Council\n  Chambers, Room A Gallery, and Studio 331 control room\n  ▪ WP5.3.2: Upgrade end-of-life network and server infrastructure\n  ▪ WP5.3.3: Upgrade and enhance enterprise software including Infor asset\n  management modules, access control systems, finance system migration,\n  meter reading infrastructure, customer management system, call center\n  software, and document management software\n\n-  SP6: Accomplish City Housing Goals\n  o G6.1: Create Opportunities for Affordable Housing\n  ▪ WP6.1.1: Pending City Council Direction Affordable housing on Gale\n  yard – enter into an agreement with a development partner and create a\n  development plan for the site\n  ▪ WP6.1.2: Pending City Council Direction Complete project entitlements\n  for affordable housing near Third and Foothill\n  ▪ WP6.1.3: Pending City Council Direction Develop design of new Public\n  Works yard (related to WP6.1.2)\n  ▪ WP6.1.4: Complete study to determine feasibility and effectiveness of\n  waiving fees and taxes for affordable housing projects\n  ▪ WP6.1.5: Complete a study of the Mixed-Use Overlay Zone, including the\n  southeast area, to recommend changes to expand and facilitate affordable\n  housing opportunities (see also WP6.3.1)\n  ▪ WP6.1.6: Continue to study opportunities for transit adjacent affordable\n  housing\n  o G6.2: Improve/maintain multifamily stock\n  ▪ WP6.2.1: Pending City Council direction Consider implementation of\n  home improvement grant/loan program or suitable alternative for low-\n  income households\n  ▪ WP6.2.2: Pending City Council direction implement proactive rental unit\n  inspection program\n\n  5\n\f  ▪ WP6.2.3: Pending City Council direction implement means-tested rent\n  subsidy program\n  o G6.3: Continue to Manage the Character of the Community\n  ▪ WP6.3.1: Complete objective design standards for residential and mixed-\n  use development\n\n-  SP7: Practice Environmental Stewardship\n  o G7.1: Increase Mobility Options and Improvements\n  ▪ WP7.1.1: Pending City Council direction Implement ongoing on-demand\n  transit service following demonstration/pilot project\n  ▪ WP7.1.2: Continue implementation of Complete Streets Plan; some\n  projects include crosswalks at the six-way intersection, Le Doux and\n  Wilshire, and pending council action on Coldwater as well as a High\n  intensity Activated crossWalK HAWK install at Wetherly/Almont and\n  Gregroy/Robertson. In addition, mid block crossings at La Cienega Park\n  on La Cienega and on La Cienega north of Wilshire being considered\n  between Wilshire and Clifton.\n  o G7.2: Reduce carbon emissions\n  ▪ WP7.2.1: Add level 2 EV chargers in City parking structures\n  ▪ WP7.2.2: Pending City Council direction Implement Climate Action and\n  Adaptation Plan (CAAP)\n  ▪ WP7.2.3: Ensure compliance with Advanced Clean Fleets Rule for vehicle\n  replacement and installation of DC Fast Chargers.\n  o G7.3: Increase water resilience\n  ▪ WP7.3.1: Implement Cabrillo pump station and forebay project to enhance\n  and increase emergency pumping capacity and redundancy\n  ▪ WP7.3.2: Implementation of citywide automated water meter multi-year\n  project\n  ▪ WP7.3.3: Complete Le Doux and Gregory Shallow Water Wells\n\n  6","minutes_text":"PK\u0003\u0004\u0014\u0000\u0006\u0000\b\u0000\u0000\u0000!\u0000�����\u0001\u0000\u0000�\n\u0000\u0000\u0013\u0000\b\u0002[Content_Types].xml �\u0004\u0002(�\u0000\u0002\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\